     "insert": "System design \u2014 overview"
    }
   ],
   "children": []
  },
  "b-dov-intro-2": {
   "id": "b-dov-intro-2",
   "type": "paragraph",
   "props": {},
   "text": [
    {
     "insert": "@codecaine-ai/canvas",
     "attributes": {
      "code": true
     }
    },
    {
     "insert": " is a typed-action, world-space diagramming engine: sticky notes, a small universal shape core, icon glyphs, sections, and routed connectors, purpose-built as Core's map layer for operational maps. The same engine embeds interactively for a person or drives headlessly for an agent. The pages in this tier are the design contracts \u2014 normative behavior, state models, and vocabularies; how the source is organized to honor them lives in the "
    },
    {
     "insert": "implementation tier",
     "attributes": {
      "reference": {
       "kind": "doc",
       "path": "20-implementation",
       "label": "implementation tier"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "insert": "."
    }
   ],
   "children": []
  },
  "b-dov-dataflow-3": {
   "id": "b-dov-dataflow-3",
   "type": "paragraph",
   "props": {},
   "text": [
    {
     "insert": "Data flows one way: every edit \u2014 a pointer gesture or an agent operation \u2014 becomes a typed "
    },
    {
     "insert": "CanvasAction",
     "attributes": {
      "code": true
     }
    },
    {
     "insert": " through the reducer, derived state (paint order, section membership) recomputes from geometry, and the stage renders what the state says. No surface writes around the reducer."
    }
   ],
   "children": []
  },
  "b-dov-reducer-decision-4": {
   "id": "b-dov-reducer-decision-4",
   "type": "decision",
   "props": {
    "status": "accepted",
    "title": "One reducer is the single mutation authority"
   },
   "text": [
    {
     "insert": "Both interactive UI actions and external agent-driven edits dispatch through the same "
    },
    {
     "insert": "reduceInteractiveCanvasState",
     "attributes": {
      "code": true,
      "reference": {
       "kind": "source",
       "path": "packages/canvas/src/state/actions/reducer.ts",
       "symbol": "reduceInteractiveCanvasState"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "insert": " reducer over the single "
    },
    {
     "insert": "CanvasAction",
     "attributes": {
      "code": true
     }
    },
    {
     "insert": " union \u2014 there is no second write path. This guarantees consistent undo/history behavior and consistent connector-waypoint reconciliation no matter which caller mutated the document, since every mutation is a typed action passing through the same authority rather than an ad hoc state patch."
    }
   ],
   "children": []
  },
  "b-dov-lightboard-decision-5": {
   "id": "b-dov-lightboard-decision-5",
   "type": "decision",
   "props": {
    "status": "accepted",
    "title": "Fixed light board background, independent of host app theme"
   },
   "text": [
    {
     "insert": "The engine renders on a fixed light background \u2014 "
    },
    {
     "insert": "CANVAS_BG = \"#F5F5F5\"",
     "attributes": {
      "code": true,
      "reference": {
       "kind": "source",
       "path": "packages/canvas/src/stage/CanvasStage.tsx",
       "symbol": "CANVAS_BG"
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "insert": " \u2014 regardless of the host app's theme. This is an intentional \"light board under dark app theme\" design choice, not an oversight: diagramming boards are conventionally light regardless of the surrounding app trim, so the canvas does not follow a host's dark-mode setting."
    }
   ],
   "children": []
  },
  "b-dov-selfcontained-6": {
   "id": "b-dov-selfcontained-6",
   "type": "paragraph",
   "props": {},
   "text": [
    {
     "insert": "Self-containment is a design commitment, not an accident of extraction: the package vendors its own UI primitives and carries no dependency back on any host app, so embedding the engine never pulls in a host's design system."
    }
   ],
   "children": []
  },
